SUMMARY:Olio Music Night: Diasporic Rhythms with Los Transplantes
DESCRIPTION:Join Los Transplantes at the Olio Lighthouse for an engaging ev
 ening of musical exploration in Afro Cuban\, Colombian\, and other South A
 merican folkloric rhythm!&nbsp\;Part concert and part lecture\, together\,
  we'll explore the intersection of artistic innovation and deep cultural t
 radition as we follow the diasporic influence of “clave” from west Afr
 ica throughout the Americas.&nbsp\; From an anthropological perspective\, 
 following the transatlantic slave trade and its unprecedented combination 
 of indigenous cultures\, learn how Los Transplantes think about traditiona
 l similarities and our global connection to rhythm. We’re all much more 
 similar than we tend to think. What does Guinean music have to do with Joh
 n Coltrane? Everything! Haitian Konpa\, Cuban Timba\, and Colombian Cumbia
 ? Yes. A lecture\, workshop\, and performance geared to be enjoyed by musi
 c enthusiasts\, beginner musicians and professionals alike! Los Transplant
 es:&nbsp\;An electrifying mix of salsa\, Cuban timba\, Afro Colombian folk
 lore\, hard hitting hip hop\, erudite jazz\, and booty shaking dance music
 \, Los Transplantes is an explosive New York City trio here to present a b
 old new soundtrack for the real all American diaspora. Musicians Puli\, Al
 ex\, and Brahm channel their extensive and diverse musical backgrounds int
 o a fiercely unified\, genre-bending sound. Their message seeks to break d
 own cultural division and deliver an undeniable celebration of unity\, hop
 e\, and resilience. The powerhouse band ignites every stage they hit\, wit
 h an infectious energy that instantly draws crowds to the dance floor\, pr
 opelling ancient tradition into a modern and accessible experience for all
  to be a part of.&nbsp\;Evening Flow7:00 PM — Doors open. Settle in\, gr
 ab a drink\, and meet a friend.7:30 PM — The evening begins: an opening 
 set with song-by-song explorations led by Los Transplantes8:30 PM — Inte
 rmission and Mingling9:00 PM — Encore!&nbsp\;10:00 PM — Last call at t
 he bar as we wind down the evening.This is a standing concert. If you need
  a seat\, reach out — we'll take care of you.What Is an Olio?Think Olio 
 is an ongoing experiment in lifelong learning. We are a community of open-
 minded people who gather to exchange ideas with new friends and connect ov
 er art\, literature\, and philosophy.Check out our full calendarOur $30 me
 mbership gives you two events for the price of one!&nbsp\;An Olio is what 
 we call the social learning events we’ve been organizing since 2015. A b
 lend between a lecture and a house party\, Olios are led by a teacher who 
 loves sharing their passions and the room is filled with curious\, open-mi
 nded New Yorkers.&nbsp\;Our goal is to spark new perspectives\, ignite cur
 iosity\, and enjoy ourselves socially—an alternative to typical nightlif
 e options.Disclaimer: By purchasing a ticket\, you agree to have your phot
 o/video used for social media/marketing materials. If you prefer to not ha
 ve your photo taken\, feel free to send us a note. Photo by Zhi-Da Zhong\n
 \nTickets & info: https://www.viewcy.com/event/olio_concert_a_globa
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/olio_concert_a_globa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8807bf0d-c254-499c-b465-b8c9fc09ccdb@viewcy.olio
DTSTAMP:20260918T162946Z
DTSTART:20261019T233000Z
DTEND:20261020T013000Z
SUMMARY:Horror Writing Workshop: The Internet Horror of Creepypastas 
DESCRIPTION:Horror Writing Workshop: The Internet Horror of Creepypastas&nb
 sp\; &nbsp\;Monday evenings at 7:30pm\, October 19th to November 30th&nbsp
 \;Join writer and professor Alexandra Dos Santos in this 6-week Olio works
 hop where you'll take inspiration from class readings and workshop your ow
 n horror stories. Each session will include lively discussion of the story
 \, and a dedicated group workshop for each writer.The creepypasta is a typ
 e of internet horror story that rose to prominence in the early days of th
 e internet. Users would “copy/paste” these stories to spread them\, cr
 eating a new genre with the iconic name “creepy pasta.” These tales bl
 urred the line between fiction and real life\; some were immersive\, pulli
 ng the reader to participate and respond online\, while others rose to fam
 e as modern urban legends.&nbsp\;Each week we'll discuss a different creep
 ypasta\, digging into what made them so spine chilling and how we can pull
  inspiration from them for our writing and our daily lives. We’ll explor
 e their unique elements\, focusing on how this medium is ripe for terror.I
 n the second half of class\, we'll workshop stories by our peers.These sto
 ries can be inspired by the creepypasta genre\, or written as general horr
 or fiction. Either way\, we'll pay tribute to the collaborative nature of 
 the creepypasta by creating\, editing\, and imagining together.&nbsp\;Each
  writer will have dedicated time for the group to closely analyze their wo
 rk and discuss possibilities for revision. You’ll walk away with a bette
 r understanding of your premise\, the heart of its fear\, and the style wi
 th which to tell it. Why write horror? Horror gives us the tools to expres
 s complex metaphysical questions\; the genre inherently questions reality 
 as we see it\, and gestures to the unseen\, the creeping\, the inescapable
 . It is the most potent genre to both transcend our humanity and dig deep 
 into it.&nbsp\;This class is for everyone: horror fanatics\, speculative w
 riters\, or those looking to try something new for spooky season. You don
 ’t need a writing background to join—just the courage to express your 
 fear through the act of writing. Whether you’re a seasoned horror writer
  or new to the genre\, you’ll feel supported in your writing in this pas
 sionate group.&nbsp\;Intimate Class of ~15 participantsMonday\, Oct 19 - &
 nbsp\;Introduction to Creepypastas\; In-class reads: “Smile Dog.jpeg” 
 and “Have you Seen this Man?”\; Writing prompts and partner feedback.&
 nbsp\;Monday\, Oct 26 - &nbsp\;Innocence Perverted: “Candle Cove”\; 3 
 workshops&nbsp\;Monday\, Nov 9 - Rituals Pastas: “The Midnight Game” 3
  workshops&nbsp\;Monday\, Nov 16 - This is a True Story “Psychosis”\; 
 3 workshops&nbsp\;Monday\, Nov 23 - The Uncanny Valley “Anasi's Goatman 
 Story”\; 3 workshops&nbsp\;Monday\, Nov 30 -&nbsp\; Urban Legends of the
  Internet: “The Russian Sleep Experiment” 3 workshopsAbout Your Instru
 ctor:Alexandra Dos Santos is a writer and College Writing instructor based
  in Astoria\, New York\, with an MFA from The Writers Foundry at St. Josep
 h's University. Her work spans horror\, the esoteric\, and the speculative
 \, appearing in Electric Literature\, Lithub\, Flash Fiction Magazine\, an
 d Vol. 1 Brooklyn\, among others. She's led creative writing workshops thr
 oughout Brooklyn and received fellowships from Wildacres Writers Retreat a
 nd the Disquiet International Literary Program.*Writers of all levels are 
 welcome here!\n\nTickets & info: https://www.viewcy.com/event/horror_writi
 ng_worksh
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/horror_writing_worksh
END:VEVENT
